WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.460
Thanks for tuning into Planetarian Daily, episode 123.

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:06.940
Today is July 17th, 2026.

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:09.100
Here's your science and health briefing.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:13.660
A new lab study shows many sweeteners alter gut bacteria growth

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:16.620
with some combinations sharply reducing diversity.

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:19.680
Researchers tested 39 sweeteners

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:21.880
and recorded more than 100 instances

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:24.460
where the compounds changed microbial growth

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:27.760
when mixed with medications, caffeine or flavorings.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:31.740
The combination of isostevial and the antidepressant

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:34.920
deloxetane stood out for cutting beneficial bacteria

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.020
and lowering overall diversity.

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:40.620
The work shows sweeteners connect directly on microbes

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:43.140
rather than only through host metabolism.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:46.720
Follow-up experiments will test whether these shifts

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:48.640
appear in human gut communities.

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:52.140
Now, shifting to a related molecular signal

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:55.280
that influences how immune cells handle aging tissue.

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:59.100
Blocking the prostate gland and EP2 receptor

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:02.040
maintain the ability of tissue resident macrophages

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:05.040
to clear senescent cells in multiple mouse organs.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:08.260
The intervention limited mitochondrial decline

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:10.420
and other age-related tissue changes.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:13.560
Restored clearance of senescent neutrophils

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:15.080
was one measurable outcome.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:17.760
Researchers will next examine whether

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:21.020
similar signaling changes occur in human aging tissues.

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:24.060
A few episodes back the show covered

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:27.180
macrophage loss of clearance capacity with age.

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:30.420
Today's blockade of this single lipid signal

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:33.640
restored neutrophil removal and protected mitochondrial

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:35.040
function across organs.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:38.420
Now, moving to another receptor level approach

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:41.020
that protects immune organ function with age.

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:44.400
Targeting the GPR-40 receptor preserved

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:46.980
thymic structure and function in older animals,

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:49.200
countering normal involution.

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:52.820
The thymus produces T cells critical for immune

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:56.720
defense. The aging cell study identifies a receptor

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:59.440
level intervention that could maintain immune capacity

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:00.080
with age.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:03.480
Next steps include testing receptor agonists

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:04.580
in additional models.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:08.000
On a different note, a living plastic material

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.980
incorporates bacteria that trigger complete breakdown

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:13.060
within six days once activated.

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:16.260
The process leaves no microplastic fragments.

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:19.420
The material targets single use applications

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:22.000
where rapid, clean degradation is needed.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:25.120
Further work will optimize bacterial strains

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:28.120
and polymer compatibility for different use cases.

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:31.220
From materials designed for controlled breakdown,

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:33.880
next comes detectors engineered for cleaner

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:35.620
performance in medical imaging.

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:39.280
The platon detector uses a light producing material,

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:42.520
a light field camera, and sensitive photon sensors

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:45.160
plus AI to map particle trajectories.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:49.160
Simulations indicate performance equal to or better

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:52.500
than current systems built from millions of separate components.

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:56.500
The design simplifies scaling and could improve resolution

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:58.340
in PET medical imaging.

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:01.680
The team plans prototype construction and validation

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:03.340
against existing detectors.

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:08.540
Finish players spend about 330 million euros yearly on golf,

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:12.320
generating an estimated 630 million euros

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:15.660
in total societal benefits according to a frontiers

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:17.860
in sports and active living analysis.

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:22.180
The study quantified health, social, and economic returns

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:23.780
beyond direct expenditures,

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:26.960
finding support continued public investment

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:28.260
in accessible courses.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:32.320
A UN report outlines practical steps for governments

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:35.440
to balance marine resource use with pollution control,

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:38.920
climate adaptation, and biodiversity protection.

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:43.440
It draws on the $2.2 trillion global ocean economy

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:46.680
and the billions of people who rely on these ecosystems.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:50.960
Authors emphasize measurable targets for pollution reduction

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:52.520
and habitat restoration.

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:56.280
Austrian research found that water-related activities

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:59.000
and access provide physical, social,

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:02.860
and psychological benefits that extend beyond exercise alone.

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:06.680
The study highlights how daily water interactions support

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:09.700
mental health and community connection in later life.

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:13.000
Results suggest urban planning should prioritize

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:15.640
safe water access for aging populations.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:19.060
University of Rhode Island surveys located

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:22.560
living freshwater muscle populations in the Moose Up River

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:25.060
for the first time in over 30 years.

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:29.100
Several native species sensitive to water quality were present.

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:32.360
Their return serves as a biological indicator

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:34.020
of improving river conditions.

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:38.700
University of Arizona tests showed graphene nano ribbons

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:41.920
retain electronic properties after exposure levels

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:44.160
relevant to fusion reactor environments.

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:47.600
The nano ribbons could serve as durable sensors

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:49.940
inside extreme radiation fields.

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:53.140
Researchers will evaluate long-term stability

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:55.780
under combined heat and radiation stress.

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:59.780
A nature reviews microbiology review synthesizes

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:02.300
evidence that warming and altered precipitation

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:05.240
change pathogen survival, transmission routes,

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:06.760
and geographic ranges.

00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:09.620
Different pathogens respond variably,

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:11.520
complicating uniform predictions.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:15.080
The analysis calls for region-specific surveillance

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:16.820
and adaptation strategies.

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:20.920
University of Seville researchers mapped microbial communities

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:24.180
along the Guadel-Kivir river to detect contamination

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:26.820
not captured by standard chemical tests.

00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:30.840
Shifts in bacterial composition flagged pollution sources

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:31.840
and gradients.

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:34.900
The approach offers a sensitive, low-cost,

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:37.460
monitoring tool for large river systems.

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:40.520
Wildfire smoke reached unhealthy levels

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:42.420
across the Midwest and East.

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:44.820
The smoke came from distant fires.

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:47.640
Visibility dropped and air quality alerts

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:50.380
were issued from the Great Lakes to the Atlantic coast.

00:05:50.840 --> 00:05:53.980
Officials advised staying indoors during peak periods.

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:58.400
MD Calc is introducing ratings for clinical calculators.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:01.780
The platform will score more than 800 tools.

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:04.400
These tools are used for risk assessment,

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:06.860
eligibility decisions, and diagnosis.

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:10.980
Scoring will focus on bias and validity criteria.

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:15.440
The system aims to help clinicians choose reliable calculators.

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:18.800
Initial ratings will cover widely used scores.

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:21.380
Plans call for ongoing updates.

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:25.580
Axiom's Whartons-Gelly derived cells produced no deaths

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:29.240
over two years in infants with severe neurological conditions.

00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:32.460
The Phase I data support the company's approach

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:33.940
to targeted brain delivery.

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:37.660
Further trials will test efficacy in larger groups.

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:42.360
The EP2 receptor findings build directly on earlier work,

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:47.040
tracking how tissue resident macrophages lose clearance capacity with age.

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:52.620
The result points to a concrete molecular handle on one driver of chronic inflammation.

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:58.600
Human tissue studies will be the clearest next indicator of whether the pathway behaves similarly.

00:06:59.380 --> 00:07:02.820
Most people assume non-caloric sweeteners pass through the body

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:05.420
without affecting anything except taste receptors.

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:10.100
In reality, they reach the colon and interact directly with resident microbes.

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:16.080
Right now, as you digest a diet drink, certain bacterial species are already adjusting

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:18.600
their growth rates in response to those compounds.

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:24.760
One lab survey found over 100 distinct interaction patterns when sweeteners were combined

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:29.920
with common drugs or flavorings, including sharp drops in microbial diversity.

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:35.240
A single memorable example is the pairing of isostavial with deloxetine,

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:39.380
which cut beneficial populations more than either substance alone.

00:07:40.340 --> 00:07:44.720
The practical takeaway is to notice how your own digestion or bowel patterns

00:07:44.720 --> 00:07:50.120
shift when you change sweetener intake, and to watch for larger human feeding studies that will

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:54.340
test whether these lab shifts translate to measurable microbiome changes.

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:59.540
New tools for tracking cellular aging and environmental exposures continue

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:02.320
to refine how we measure daily health influences.

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:08.440
Keep an eye on upcoming human tissue studies that will test whether the EP2 pathway behaves

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:12.320
similarly in people. That's Planetarian Daily for today.

